  "live_records": {
    "q-25233": {
      "dom_id": "step-q25233",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Express ${log}_{2}⁡({x}^{3})-{log}_{2}⁡(x)$ as a single logarithm.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the quotient rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}⁡(a)-{log}_{n}⁡(b)={log}_{n}⁡(\\frac{a}{b})\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule for logarithms, the given expression can be rewritten as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{3})-{log}_{2}⁡(x) & ={log}_{2}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x}) \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
