    "q-66765": {
      "dom_id": "step-q66765",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Express ${log}_{2}⁡(7)-{log}_{2}⁡(5)$ as a single logarithm.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the quotient rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}⁡(a)-{log}_{n}⁡(b)={log}_{n}⁡(\\frac{a}{b})\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule for logarithms, the given expression can be rewritten as:\n\n$$\n{log}_{2}⁡(7)-{log}_{2}⁡(5)={log}_{2}⁡(\\frac{7}{5})\n$$",
