    "q-66772": {
      "dom_id": "step-q66772",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$6{log}_{5}⁡(100)-6{log}_{5}⁡(4)=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the quotient rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}⁡(a)-{log}_{n}⁡(b)={log}_{n}⁡(\\frac{a}{b})\n$$\n\nIf we factor the given expression and use the quotient rule for logarithms, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{log}_{5}⁡(100)-6{log}_{5}⁡(4) & =6({log}_{5}⁡(100)-{log}_{5}⁡(4)) \\\\  & =6{log}_{5}⁡(\\frac{100}{4}) \\\\  & =6{log}_{5}⁡(25)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${5}^{2}=25$, then ${log}_{5}⁡(25)={log}_{5}⁡({5}^{2})=2.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n6{log}_{5}⁡(25)=6\\cdot 2=12.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
