    "q-99953": {
      "dom_id": "step-q99953",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Express $6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(68)-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(17)$ as a single logarithm.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the quotient rule for natural logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡(a)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(b)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{a}{b})\n$$\n\nIf we factor the given expression and use the quotient rule for logarithms, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(68)-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(17) & =6(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(68)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(17)) \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{68}{17}) \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(68)-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(17)=6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
