      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "${log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the quotient rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}⁡(a)-{log}_{n}⁡(b)={log}_{n}⁡(\\frac{a}{b})\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule for logarithms, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}) & ={log}_{3}⁡(x)-{log}_{3}⁡(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
