    "q-47298": {
      "dom_id": "step-q47298",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{3}}{8})=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the quotient rule for natural logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡(a)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(b)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{a}{b})\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule for natural logarithms, the given expression can be rewritten as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{3}}{8}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) \\\\  & =3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
