    "q-108201": {
      "dom_id": "step-q108201",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "If $\\operatorname{log}⁡(y)=k$ and $\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})=m$, then $\\operatorname{log}⁡(x)=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the quotient rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}⁡(a)-{log}_{n}⁡(b)={log}_{n}⁡(\\frac{a}{b})\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule for logarithms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(x) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{y}{(\\frac{y}{x})}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =k-m.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
