    "q-24442": {
      "dom_id": "step-q24442",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "If $\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)=p$ and $\\operatorname{log}⁡(y)=q$, then $\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{2}{y})=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the quotient rule for common logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡(a)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(b)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{a}{b})\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule for common logarithms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{2}{y}) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(y) \\\\  & =p-q\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
